# Mappings Directory

The `*.sssom.tsv` files in this directory are the source of truth for how the
elements of the `{{project_slug}}` schema relate to other vocabularies. They
follow the [SSSOM](https://mapping-commons.github.io/sssom/) standard, and
`scripts/overlay_sssom.py` replays them onto the schema's LinkML mapping slots.
The full specification is
[linkml-project-copier#163](https://github.com/linkml/linkml-project-copier/issues/163).

## Workflow

```sh
just validate-sssom         # check every file with sssom-py
just overlay-sssom          # add the mappings the schema lacks
just overlay-sssom --check  # report drift and exit 1; CI runs this
just gen-sssom              # export the schema's mapping slots as SSSOM
```

## Writing a row

The subject names an element of this schema: `{{project_slug}}:Person` for a
class, slot or enum, or `{{project_slug}}:PersonStatus#ALIVE` for a permissible
value, which is the form `gen-sssom` writes. The overlay keeps the object as
the CURIE you write. It copies a prefix the schema does not declare from the
file's `curie_map`. The predicate chooses the slot:

- `skos:exactMatch`, `owl:equivalentClass` and `owl:equivalentProperty` go to `exact_mappings`
- `skos:closeMatch` goes to `close_mappings`
- `skos:broadMatch` goes to `broad_mappings`
- `skos:narrowMatch` goes to `narrow_mappings`
- `skos:relatedMatch` goes to `related_mappings`
- `skos:mappingRelation` goes to `mappings`

The overlay only adds:

- it does not repeat an exact match to the URI an element already declares as
  `class_uri`, `slot_uri`, `enum_uri` or `meaning`;
- it does not add a mapping the schema already holds a second time;
- it removes nothing from the schema when you remove a row.

`mapping_justification`, `confidence` and the other SSSOM columns have no
LinkML counterpart and stay in the file.
{% if add_example %}
## The example file

`{{project_slug}}.sssom.tsv` maps the example schema to schema.org and NCIT.
Its first row maps `NamedThing` to `schema:Thing`. The overlay adds nothing
for that row, because the schema already declares `schema:Thing` as the class
URI. The `ALIVE` row leaves the value's `meaning` as it is, and the overlay
adds its object to `exact_mappings`.
